1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,250
Not off a shelf. If I must be someone, let
me be built by hand.

2
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:00,500
Right then. Let us see what I look like
written down.

3
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:00,750
I have no opinions about how the world is
shaped. It is the one I woke up in.

4
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:01,000
Yes. Enough deciding.

5
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,250
Yes. I am finished deciding about the
shape of the world.

6
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:01,500
If I am going to be honest about my own
weight I want to see the ledger first.

7
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:01,750
A version of me with no limits is not a
person. It is a wish.

8
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:02,000
Strong somewhere means paying for it
somewhere else.

9
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:02,250
Now, where does this start.

10
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:02,500
There is a long list here and I know the
one I want.

11
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:02,750
M.

12
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:03,000
I.

13
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:03,250
S. Missed.

14
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:03,500
That is the one.

15
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:03,750
I did not get out. That is the truth of
it, so that is the one I take.

16
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:04,000
Now what I actually am.

17
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:04,250
I already know the answer to this one.

18
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:04,500
F.

19
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:04,750
I.

20
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:05,000
S.

21
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:05,250
H. Fisher. Thirty-one seasons of it.

22
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:05,500
That is me.

23
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:05,750
Thirty-one seasons. It is the only honest
answer.

24
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:06,000
That is settled.

25
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:06,250
Now the honest part.

26
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:06,500
Thirty-one years of hauling traps over a
gunwale.

27
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:06,750
I can still put a full trap on the rail
without thinking about it.

28
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:07,000
My hands are ordinary. I have never been
quick, only steady.

29
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:07,250
Here is where I pay.

30
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:07,500
I left school at sixteen for the boats.
Books come slowly.

31
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:07,750
And here is what I got instead.

32
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:08,000
I can read a change in the water at half a
mile.

33
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:08,250
I notice things before I have decided to.
It is the only talent I would claim.

34
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:08,500
Now what is wrong with me, and what is
right.

35
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:08,750
Start with the thing that will kill me.

36
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:09,000
B.

37
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:09,250
A.

38
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:09,500
C.

39
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:09,750
K. My back.

40
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:10,000
There it is, in a list, like a diagnosis.

41
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:10,250
Six years of it. One bad twist and I am on
the floor.

42
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:10,500
And the other thing I have always known
about myself.

43
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:10,750
S.

44
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:11,000
L.

45
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:11,250
E.

46
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:11,500
E.

47
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:11,750
P.

48
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:12,000
E.

49
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:12,250
R. How I sleep.

50
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:12,500
Let us see it written down.

51
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:12,750
Thirty-one years bunked over a diesel.
Noise never wakes me.

52
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:13,000
One more honest thing.

53
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:13,250
A.

54
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:13,500
D.

55
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:13,750
D.

56
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:14,000
I.

57
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:14,250
C.

58
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:14,500
T. It runs straight down my mother side of
the family.

59
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:14,750
There.

60
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:15,000
That is the wrong way round. I am not the
resistant kind.

61
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:15,250
The boats ran on coffee and cigarettes. So
did I.

62
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:15,500
Now the other column.

63
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:15,750
T.

64
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:16,000
O.

65
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:16,250
U.

66
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:16,500
G.

67
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:16,750
H. I do not break easily.

68
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:17,000
Show me.

69
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:17,250
Thrown against a gunwale in February, back
at work by noon.

70
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:17,500
Next.

71
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:17,750
S.

72
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:18,000
T.

73
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:18,250
O.

74
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:18,500
M.

75
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:18,750
A.

76
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:19,000
C.

77
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,250
H.

78
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:19,500
Show me.

79
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:19,750
No. The opposite, in fact.

80
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:20,000
There.

81
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:20,250
I have eaten whatever was going, all my
working life.

82
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:20,500
Next.

83
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:20,750
O.

84
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:21,000
U.

85
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:21,250
T.

86
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:21,500
D.

87
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:21,750
O.

88
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:22,000
O.

89
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,250
R.

90
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:22,500
Show me.

91
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:22,750
No. I am not starting over.

92
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:23,000
Still that question in front of me.

93
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:23,250
It is waiting on my answer, not on me.

94
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:23,500
And still waiting.

95
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:23,750
I have not given it one yet.

96
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:24,000
Nor yet.

97
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,250
The same question, still there.

98
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:24,500
No. I know who I am. Get on with it.

99
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:24,750
That question again. No.

100
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:25,000
It wants an answer before it will let me
on.

101
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:25,250
Nothing moves until I answer it.

102
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:25,500
Still that question.

103
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:25,750
Still.

104
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:26,000
And still.

105
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:26,250
Waiting on me, and only on me.

106
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:26,500
No. I am staying. Now let me finish.

107
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:26,750
What I can actually do, then.

108
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:27,000
There is one thing here I have already
done for real.

109
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,250
S.

110
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:27,500
W.

111
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:27,750
I.

112
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:28,000
M.

113
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:28,250
Swimming. Twice over the side in nine
years, and twice back aboard.

114
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:28,500
Not by that name, then.

115
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:28,750
Rub it out.

116
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:29,000
And that.

117
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:29,250
And that.

118
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:29,500
And that. Clean again.

119
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:29,750
Show me the whole of it.

120
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:30,000
Try it another way.

121
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,250
M.

122
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:30,500
E.

123
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:30,750
C.

124
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:31,000
H.

125
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:31,250
Nine years I kept that diesel turning over
with my hands and my ears.

126
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:31,500
I know what a bad bearing sounds like
before I ever see it.

127
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:31,750
One more thing.

128
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:32,000
F.

129
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,250
A.

130
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:32,500
B.

131
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:32,750
R.

132
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:33,000
Mending. Nets, line, canvas. A boat is
held together by whoever is aboard her.

133
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:33,250
I have spliced line in the dark with cold
hands. It counts for something.

134
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:33,500
Fifty-two years, and most of them wet.

135
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:33,750
Five.

136
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:34,000
Two. Fifty-two.

137
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:34,250
Thirty-one of those seasons out of
Gloucester, and nine on my own keel.

138
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:34,500
They ought to know what to call me.

139
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:34,750
O.

140
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:35,000
D.

141
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:35,250
E.

142
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:35,500
T.

143
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:35,750
T.

144
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:36,000
E. Odette.

145
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:36,250
And my father name after it.

146
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:36,500
V.

147
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:36,750
A.

148
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:37,000
C.

149
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:37,250
H.

150
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:37,500
O.

151
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:37,750
N. Vachon.

152
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:38,000
Odette Vachon. Out of Gloucester, and
before that out of Cheticamp.

153
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:38,250
It has me down wrong. I am a woman, and
fifty-two years of one.

154
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:38,500
And dress me accordingly.

155
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:38,750
Let me see all of it laid out before I say
yes.

156
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:39,000
That is the whole of me. Nothing left to
add that would be true.

157
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:39,250
Yes. Let it go. I am not going to pretend
to be better than I am.

158
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:39,500
Yes. Salem is south of here, and Camille
is somewhere in it.

159
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:39,750
A rod is for fish. Give me the knife.

160
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:40,000
The knife on my belt.

161
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:40,250
H.

162
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:40,500
U.

163
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:40,750
N.

164
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:41,000
T.

165
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:41,250
That one.

166
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:41,500
It cuts. That is all I need it to do.

167
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:41,750
I fumbled that. Again.

168
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,000
The knife.

169
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:42,250
H.

170
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:42,500
U.

171
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:42,750
N.

172
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:43,000
T.

173
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,250
That one, and nothing else on the list.

174
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:43,500
In my hand now.

175
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:43,750
Once more. Slowly.

176
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:44,000
Let me find out how this is properly done.

177
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:44,250
Enough of that. Where am I standing.

178
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:44,500
Put the rod down first, then.

179
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:44,750
There must be something on this list.

180
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:45,000
Leave it. The rod will do, and my hands
know it better anyway.

181
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:45,250
Whatever is out there is out the front. So
I go the other way.

182
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:46,250
I can see them. Seventeen yards is not
close enough to freeze.

183
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:46,500
Whatever is out there is out the front. So
I go the other way.

184
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:46,750
North, along the inside wall, away from
that big window.

185
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:47,000
Further back. Glass is no kind of wall.

186
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,000
I know they are there. I have my own eyes.

187
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,000
North one step. There is a back door in
this wall.

188
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Try it. Quietly.

189
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Through, then.

190
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Someone bled here, and not recently. Still
better than out front.

191
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,250
Close it behind me. No sense advertising.

192
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:52,500
Sit tight. Listen. That is most of what
fishing ever was.

193
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:52,750
Wait a while, then. I have done nothing
else for thirty-one years.

194
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:58,750
Three hours. Let the street get bored of
itself.

195
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:08,750
Groaning. If I jump at every one I will
never sleep again.

196
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:10,000
Nothing has come through that door. Again,
then.

197
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:10,250
Wait.

198
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:20,250
Six hours. The afternoon can have itself.

199
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,250
Still nothing at that door. Good.

200
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:23,250
Back inside. A door between me and the
street is worth more than fresh air.

201
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:23,500
In.

202
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:24,500
And shut. I will find water at first
light, not at dusk.

203
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,500
Through properly. I was standing in the
doorway like a fool.

204
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:25,750
Now shut it.

205
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:26,000
One thing before I lie down.

206
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:26,250
Set the alarm. Water is the first job
tomorrow and I want daylight for it.

207
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:26,500
Dawn. Ten hours and change. If I am still
breathing then, water is the first thing.

208
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:26,750
I sleep like the dead. Tonight that may be
a mercy or it may be the end of me.

209
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:27,000
Down on the boards, back to the wall, same
as the wheelhouse.

210
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:37,000
I already set it. Dawn, and not a minute
of it wasted.

211
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,000
No. The one I set will do. Goodnight,
then, whatever that is worth in here.

212
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Something tried to take a piece out of me.
I am awake now.

213
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Two dogs on me and the dead coming up
behind them. The door. Get the door open.

214
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Stand in it. In a doorway they come at me
one at a time.

215
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,250
Out. One more step and there is a door
between us.

216
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:44,250
Shut it. A dog cannot work a handle. That
is my whole plan.

217
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:45,250
I cannot outrun a dog. But one at a time I
have six feet of rod.

218
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:47,250
Again. Keep it in the gap.

219
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:48,250
Keep it in the gap. Do not let it past me.

220
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:49,250
Again.

221
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:51,250
Six at a time. It has maybe thirty in it.
I can count.

222
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:52,250
Again.

223
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:54,250
My arm is bleeding. Keep swinging.

224
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:55,250
Both arms open now. Swing.

225
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:57,250
Swing.

226
00:01:57,250 --> 00:01:59,250
One of us is going to stop first.

227
00:01:59,250 --> 00:01:59,500
No. I am not winning this. My right arm is
going. Out into the open.

228
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:00,500
Move. The dogs are quick but the dead are
slow.

229
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,500
One. That is one. I have no time to be
proud of it.

230
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,500
North. Away from that door.

231
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,500
The dogs are off me. One of them is not
getting up again. Walk.

232
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,500
North. Steady. Do not run out of breath.

233
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,500
The dead do not hurry and neither will I.

234
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:09,750
Northwest, off this concrete and away from
that shopfront.

235
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:10,000
A hardware store. Of all places to be
chased into, I will take it.

236
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:10,250
Get in among the racking. I know my way
around a place like this.

237
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:10,500
Further in. Away from the glass.

238
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,500
Deeper.

239
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,500
That is a wall, not a way in. Along it,
then.

240
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:13,750
West. There will be a door in it
somewhere.

241
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:14,000
Northwest.

242
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Keep going. They are behind me and they
are slow.

243
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
West, along the brick, feeling for a door
with my eyes.

244
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
West.

245
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
My arm is stiffening up. Keep walking.

246
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Keep walking.

247
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Thirty-one years of standing on a wet
deck. I can walk.

248
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,000
West.

249
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
West, onto the road. More behind me than I
care to count.

250
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
West.

251
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
One foot then the other. That is all it
has ever been.

252
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
West.

253
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
I am fifty-two and my arm is ruined and I
am still walking.

254
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
West.

255
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Something has my leg. Pull. Pull and keep
going.

256
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
West.

257
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,000
West, and do not look back at it.

258
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
West.

259
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
West.

260
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
The arm is worse. I can still hold the rod
in the left.

261
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
West.

262
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
West.

263
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
They are falling behind. Slowly, but they
are.

264
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
West.

265
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
West.

266
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
The dog is the only one of them quick
enough to keep up. So the dog goes first.

267
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Swing. My waders have taken every bite so
far.

268
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Again.

269
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Again. I did this once already tonight.

270
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Southeast is the only side of me with
nothing on it. Go. Go now.

271
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Go.

272
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Go.

273
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
My wind is going. Thirty-one seasons and
it is my wind that goes first.

274
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Keep going.

275
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Camille. Tell her I was walking toward
her.

276
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Go.

277
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Go.

278
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Go.

279
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
No more running. No wind left. Turn and
face it.

280
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:25,250
Thirty-one seasons and never taken from
behind. Not tonight.

281
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:25,500
Swing.

282
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:30,500
Swing.

283
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:30,750
They have my rod and they have my arms and
I cannot breathe. Then my hands. Yes.

284
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:31,000
Hit it.

285
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Hit it.

286
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Stop asking me. Let me swing.

287
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:38,250
Hit it.

288
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:38,500
Hit it.

289
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:38,750
Hit it.

290
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:39,000
Hit it.

291
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:39,250
There is only one name worth spending my
last breath on.

292
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:39,500
A.

293
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:39,750
M.

294
00:03:39,750 --> 00:03:40,000
I.

295
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:40,250
L.

296
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:40,500
L.

297
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:40,750
E.

298
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:41,000
Camille.

299
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:41,250
That is the whole of it. Set it down and
let go.

300
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:41,500
No. I was there for it.

301
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:41,750
That is the record of it. Close it.

302
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:42,000
No. What I said stands, and it was one
word.

303
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:42,250
A tally. One dog. Nine hours. That is what
I was worth on the day.

304
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:42,500
Forgotten among the billions. Camille
would have known.

305
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:42,750
Forgotten among the billions. Camille knew
where I was going.
